The '''Team Rocket Academy''' (Japanese: '''ロケット団特別訓練所''' ''Team Rocket Special Training Center'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive location likely in [[Kanto]]. It was featured in ''[[HS12|Training Daze]]''. The academy is the place where people train to become members of [[Team Rocket]]. They undergo training and develop skills such as stealthy stealing, tracking and capturing Pokémon. The campus is a large building containing training rooms, shower rooms, bedrooms, and a nursery. The head of the Team Rocket Academy is {{an|Giovanni}}, while the Drill Sergeant is [[Viper]].

The Team Rocket Academy is where [[Jessie]], [[James]] and {{MTR}} were grouped together and became official members of Team Rocket and partners, while their rivals, [[Butch]], [[Cassidy]], and {{p|Raticate}} were also grouped together and became official members of Team Rocket.
[[File:Team Rocket Noodle Bar.png|thumb|left|250px|Team Rocket's Noodle Bar outside the Academy]]
The Team Rocket Academy was mentioned in passing in ''[[DP047|Sandshrew's Locker!]]'' when [[Mira]] told {{TRT}} she wanted to join.

In ''[[DP092|A Lean Mean Team Rocket Machine!]]'', James used his training at Team Rocket Academy, prior to being partnered with Jessie, as motivation to work as hard as possible.

In a flashback in ''[[DP117|Noodles! Roamin' Off!]]'', {{OBP|Christopher|DP117}} was training for Team Rocket, with little success. Jessie and James bought him a bowl of ramen noodles at a noodle bar to cheer him up, and that motivated him to leave Team Rocket and start a noodle restaurant.
